{"name":"PSL scale","deep":true,"image":null,"mentions":54,"casual":{"lead":["PSL, short for Perceived Sexual Levels, is an informal scale looksmaxxing communities use to rate male faces, usually from 1 to 8. It gives members a common benchmark and a target to aim for when they change skin, hair, leanness or style.","It sets out tiers from below average through normie and Chadlite up to Chad and beyond. Raters judge faces on features grouped under harmony, dimorphism, angularity and individual features. Its name is said to combine three forums where it arose, and no published study has evaluated the scale itself."],"sections":[{"h":"How people use it","paras":["People post photos for ratings, note their tier, then repost after changes such as a haircut, clearer skin or fat loss to see how opinions shift. Because raters differ, many collect several opinions."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Risks & side effects","paras":["The scale carries no physical risk. It is subjective and not scientifically validated, and commentators cited by Wikipedia link the surrounding culture of tiering people to body dysmorphia and distress."],"subs":[]}]},"gallery":[],"links":{"studies":[{"title":"A chemosensory system that regulates biofilm formation through modulation of cyclic diguanylate levels.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16186483/","source":"Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences of the United States of America","year":2005,"cites":625,"kind":null},{"title":"PTEN: one gene, many syndromes.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12938083/","source":"Human mutation","year":2003,"cites":552,"kind":"Review"},{"title":"Tabix: fast retrieval of sequence features from generic TAB-delimited files.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21208982/","source":"Bioinformatics (Oxford, England)","year":2011,"cites":529,"kind":null},{"title":"Pel is a cationic exopolysaccharide that cross-links extracellular DNA in the Pseudomonas aeruginosa biofilm matrix.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26311845/","source":"Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences of the United States of America","year":2015,"cites":482,"kind":null},{"title":"The Pel and Psl polysaccharides provide Pseudomonas aeruginosa structural redundancy within the biofilm matrix.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22176658/","source":"Environmental microbiology","year":2012,"cites":458,"kind":null},{"title":"Assembly and development of the Pseudomonas aeruginosa biofilm matrix.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/19325879/","source":"PLoS pathogens","year":2009,"cites":448,"kind":null},{"title":"Pseudomonas biofilm matrix composition and niche biology.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22212072/","source":"FEMS microbiology reviews","year":2012,"cites":436,"kind":"Review"},{"title":"Pseudomonas aeruginosa uses a cyclic-di-GMP-regulated adhesin to reinforce the biofilm extracellular matrix.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20088866/","source":"Molecular microbiology","year":2010,"cites":419,"kind":null},{"title":"Biosynthesis of the Pseudomonas aeruginosa Extracellular Polysaccharides, Alginate, Pel, and Psl.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21991261/","source":"Frontiers in microbiology","year":2011,"cites":406,"kind":"review-article"},{"title":"The pel polysaccharide can serve a structural and protective role in the biofilm matrix of Pseudomonas aeruginosa.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21298031/","source":"PLoS pathogens","year":2011,"cites":405,"kind":null},{"title":"Role of polysaccharides in Pseudomonas aeruginosa biofilm development.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17981495/","source":"Current opinion in microbiology","year":2007,"cites":387,"kind":"Review"},{"title":"Two genetic loci produce distinct carbohydrate-rich structural components of the Pseudomonas aeruginosa biofilm matrix.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15231777/","source":"Journal of bacteriology","year":2004,"cites":376,"kind":null}],"trials":[],"la